{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/523734-forsaken-without-the-alpha-theory","id":523734,"title":"Forsaken without the Alpha theory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-21T15:19:03-07:00","id":523734,"title":"Forsaken without the Alpha theory","content":"Forsaken packs seems to be based on the premise that a single alpha wins a dominance contest to become alpha and rule the pack. Based on more recent studies, that seems to be an inaccurate depiction of a wolf pack. <a href=\"http://io9.com/why-everything-you-know-about-wolf-packs-is-wrong-502754629\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/why-everything-you-kn...rong-502754629</a> Instead a wolf pack seems to just be a family with pups eventually breaking off and forming new packs. Is there a way to instead apply this pack mentality to forsaken and would it change anything essential to the pack? Possibly a pack operating more with two older veteran wolves and adopted pack members who eventually break off on their own. Or maybe having werewolf packs tied strongly to familial bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:28:35-07:00","id":523757,"title":"","content":"Werewolves aren't wolves. They presumably follow the setup because that's how Father Wolf did it.<br /> <br /> Having it run another way wouldn't require any changes except possibly getting rid of the Alpha Gifts. Protectorates are a different way of doing things, and first edition notes many other set ups, including the odd democracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T16:24:01-07:00","id":523779,"title":"","content":"Well, the dominance-based pack behavior is what happens with Wolves in captivity, so it actually makes a lot of sense that werewolf packs reflected that in 1e, since they couldn't mate with each other and form &quot;proper&quot; familial packs. Now that Uratha can breed freely in 2e, familial packs are actually possible. And appropriately, the idea of pack alphas isn't actually brought up in the 2e core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:09:59-07:00","id":523911,"title":"","content":"Uratha can breed freely now? I must have missed that...<br /> <br /> And suddenly I can't help but imagine dominance-based werewolf packs as some kind of kinky BDSM communes. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:54:06-07:00","id":523943,"title":"","content":"I would reasume the Alpha Theory could return in the Pure Tribes - they ideology say they are &quot;cast away&quot; from Pangea Paradise, are &quot;locked&quot; in this fallen reality - and they are based on Hatred Ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:56:34-07:00","id":523944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/523734-forsaken-without-the-alpha-theory?p=523911#post523911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha can breed freely now? I must have missed that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The Oath still states <i>The Uratha Shall Cleave to the Human</i>, but literally the first sentence discussing that tenant in the Oath of the Moon section says &quot;Uratha mate among themselves and humans.&quot;<br /> <br /> The astute observer will notice that the Oath doesn't say <i>The Uratha Shall Not Pork The Uratha</i>. It exists to ensure werewolves maintain social ties to humanity, not dictate who they can sleep with. And since the Unihar are no longer a problem, there's nothing stopping werewolves from having children. Those children aren't guaranteed to be werewolves of course, but there's a good chance of them at least being Wolf-Blooded, and humans and Wolf-Bloods are allowed in packs now, you can totally make family packs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/523734-forsaken-without-the-alpha-theory?p=523911#post523911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And suddenly I can't help but imagine dominance-based werewolf packs as some kind of kinky BDSM communes. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this has to happen now. Next time I get to run werewolf, I'm making an NPC pack where all of the members are part of a kinky poly family, with the primary Dom as the alpha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T23:49:19-07:00","id":524069,"title":"","content":"A few packs probably have no official structure but there's still this one guy who everyone looks to in a crisis. <br /> <br /> Like, &quot;We don't have an Alpha but it's totally Dave.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T00:05:53-07:00","id":524135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/523734-forsaken-without-the-alpha-theory?p=524069#post524069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few packs probably have no official structure but there's still this one guy who everyone looks to in a crisis.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;We don't have an Alpha but it's totally Dave.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or switch who is considered the 'alpha' based off of who has the skills and expertise most relevant to the current situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T02:08:10-07:00","id":524189,"title":"","content":"I think it's safe to say that there are almost as many pack structure models as there are packs. Some will have absolute alpha, others will have rotating alpha, some will be anarchist and do everything by consensus or individually etc.<br /> <br /> In other words, go nuts with designing whatever fits your setting. I applaud non-typical pack models; they're interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T11:39:13-07:00","id":524596,"title":"","content":"You may not address the ones who call the shots in a familial pack 'alpha' male or female, but families do, indeed, have patriarchs and/or matriarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:20:14-07:00","id":524620,"title":"","content":"Plus having one person lead makes things simple in tense situations, where you don't have time to debate options or take a vote.<br /> <br /> Though it can be bad if said 'alpha' sucks at decision-making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T13:00:51-07:00","id":524676,"title":"","content":"I think it's just a matter of how the leader got their authority. In forced packs, it's usually earned through competition and maintained through reinforcing dominance. In familial packs, the parents are pretty much the leaders by default because they're the most experienced. Obviously werewolves, with their human-like brains and social experience will bring their own social structures to their packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:38:27-07:00","id":545405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/523734-forsaken-without-the-alpha-theory?p=524676#post524676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's just a matter of how the leader got their authority. In forced packs, it's usually earned through competition and maintained through reinforcing dominance. In familial packs, the parents are pretty much the leaders by default because they're the most experienced. Obviously werewolves, with their human-like brains and social experience will bring their own social structures to their packs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's the key there. The idea of an &quot;alpha&quot; is the human side coming out instead of the wolf side. I'm sure many packs do have leaders who exert dominance to varying degrees, but that's because that invariably happens when you have a group of humans, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:02:04-07:00","id":547492,"title":"","content":"Rose Bailey (i think that's who it was) said in some other thread to me that you didn't have to use the Alpha thing if you didn't want to and the game should work fine. Your player's pack can decide things however the want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:25:25-07:00","id":548803,"title":"","content":"The only time that the Alpha thing comes up, in my opinion, is when we start talking about 1) the Dominance Gifts, and 2) Spirit Rank. It feels like the spirit hierarchy in the Hisil is now entirely based on the Alpha-theory situation, so, as the werewolves are necessarily part of it, they can't get away from it when dealing with spirits.<br /> <br /> With Dominance Gifts, its only Honor and Purity aspects. You do what I say, because I'm Dominant to you (though, lets be fair, we can have PCs that have the gifts but don't use them on pack). And its not so much that you are dominant to another, as you try to force that Dominance onto someone else, designated &quot;prey.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neither of the above are forced to apply to inter-pack relations, but absolutely with pack-v-everyone else. And its very easy to go both ways.<br /> <br /> EDIT - oh, a third and fourth way. Dalu's Badass Motherfucker trait - use your presence to force someone to give another up. Another I'm-the-dominant-one-here thing. Again, still no requirement to actually use it on another wolf. The Rahu can inflict Submissive on prey, but again, no promise of using it on fellow wolves. If anything, that last one is discouraged from use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-10-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}